      "content": "That \"focused, in-depth analysis\" angle sounds good. Like we're doing a deep dive rather than just having a small group. \n\nBut if I write that we chose this approach to gain \"rigorous examination,\" isn't that a bit of a stretch? Technically, we just didn't have the budget/access to get more people. Do you think we can get away with presenting it as a strategic methodological decision to prioritize data quality over quantity, or will that look like we're trying to hide the actual constraints?",
